+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema as its `inputSchema`, and that schema is handed verbatim to the providers to shape what the model sends. `ToolRegistry.execute` holds the input the model actually sent to that same schema before the executor runs, so a malformed call fails in one predictable way — as a tool result the model can read and correct — instead of reaching an executor that has to guess, or ending the conversation with a transport error.
+
+## Contract of `ToolRegistry.execute`
+
+- Input the declared schema rejects is answered with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing required property, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: returns a rejection naming the missing required property and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L30)).
+- A rejection names the failing property path and the constraint that failed, and neither the returned text nor any log line carries a property value, because tool input is where identifying data enters the engine ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field by path and expected type without echoing any input value into the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L43)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled when it is registered, so a schema that cannot compile throws from `register` with a message naming the tool, at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L65)).
+- A rejection is a tool result rather than an exception: the tool loop carries it to the provider on the next round, a corrected retry reaches the executor with its input unchanged, extra properties included, and `processMessage` resolves ([validated by: resolves after a rejected call and a corrected retry, showing the rejection to the provider and passing the retry through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L78)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` only; it does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types or apply defaults, and there is no opt-out.
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once, not once per call.
+- A schema produced by a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is resolved and validated per call, against the schema current at that call rather than a stale cached one.
+- An unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`; returning it to the model instead is a separate issue.
+- The tool-round bound (`DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS`) is what stops a model that keeps sending rejected input from retrying forever.
